    {
      "id": 4,
      "narration": "Let's look at the four most common types. First, we have int for whole numbers. Then char for a single letter. Notice how we use single quotes for the letter A. This is important.",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "TypingCode",
        "type_anchor": "First,",
        "props": {
          "filename": "Main.java",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "public class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) {\n    int age = 25;\n    char grade = 'A';\n    System.out.println(age);\n    System.out.println(grade);\n  }\n}",
          "highlightLines": [
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        "camera": [
          {
            "at": "int",
            "zoom": 1.6,
            "x": 50,
            "y": 35
          }
        ],
        "popups": [
          {
            "anchor": "quotes",
            "text": "Single quotes for char",
            "kind": "tip"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "narration": "When we run this code, the compiler looks for the variable named age and finds the number twenty-five. Then it finds the grade and prints the character A to the console.",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "TerminalRun",
        "props": {
          "command": "java Main.java",
          "output": [
            "25",
            "A"
          ]
        },
        "camera": [
          {
            "at": "run",
            "zoom": 1.4,
            "x": 50,
            "y": 50
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "narration": "Now, what if we need decimals? We use the double type. And for yes or no questions, we use boolean. A boolean can only be true or false. It is like a light switch.",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "TypingCode",
        "type_anchor": "Now,",
        "props": {
          "filename": "Main.java",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "double price = 19.99;\nboolean isJavaFun = true;\nSystem.out.println(price);\nSystem.out.println(isJavaFun);",
          "highlightLines": [
            1,
            2
          ]
        },
        "previous_code": "public class Main {\n  public static void main(String[] args) {\n    int age = 25;\n    char grade = 'A';\n    System.out.println(age);\n    System.out.println(grade);\n  }\n}",
        "camera": [
          {
            "at": "double",
            "zoom": 1.7,
            "x": 50,
            "y": 30
          }
        ],
        "popups": [
          {
