    {
      "id": 8,
      "narration": "You might wonder why we have both int and double. Use int for things you count, like people or apples. Use double for measurements, like weight or money, where precision matters.",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "ComparisonCard",
        "props": {
          "title": "int vs double",
          "leftTitle": "int (Integer)",
          "leftPoints": [
            "Whole numbers only",
            "No decimal points",
            "Example: 10, -5, 0"
          ],
          "rightTitle": "double",
          "rightPoints": [
            "Decimal numbers",
            "High precision",
            "Example: 10.5, 3.14"
          ]
        },
        "keyIdea": "Whole numbers vs Decimals"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "narration": "Watch out for this common mistake. If you try to put a decimal number into an int box, Java will get angry. It refuses to throw away the decimal part without your permission.",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "TypingCode",
        "type_anchor": "Watch",
        "props": {
          "filename": "Error.java",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "int score = 95.5;",
          "highlightLines": [
            1
          ]
        },
        "camera": [
          {
            "at": "angry",
            "zoom": 1.8,
            "x": 50,
            "y": 20
          }
        ],
        "popups": [
          {
            "anchor": "mistake",
            "text": "Cannot fit 0.5 in int",
            "kind": "tip"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "narration": "When you try to compile this, you will see an error saying 'possible lossy conversion'. This is Java's way of saying, 'Hey, you are going to lose that point five!'",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "TerminalRun",
        "props": {
          "command": "javac Error.java",
          "output": [
            "Error.java:1: error: incompatible types:",
            "possible lossy conversion from double to int",
            "int score = 95.5;",
            "            ^"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "narration": "To recap, use int for whole numbers, double for decimals, char for single characters, and boolean for logic. Practice task: create a variable for your height in feet. Which type should you use?",
      "remotion": {
        "type": "SummaryList",
        "props": {
          "title": "Quick Checklist",
          "items": [
